-| Map key rule | `K` and `T` must be data by the `value` rule of `dataOnly`, because `Equal` compares a function, an Effect, a Ref and a Stream by reference. A key or an element that is not data is `declaration/019`. A record key is allowed, because `Equal` and `Hash` compare a record by structure. The check waits until every declaration of the module is defined, so a key may name a later type. `V` can be any type. A `Map` or `Set` of data is data, so it can be a record field, a tagged record field, an error field, an exported contract and a host interface type. A `Map` whose value holds a function type in a tagged record or an error field is `declaration/015`. The independent validator rejects a forged `map` or `set` type whose key is not data | [type_lower.ts](../src/core/type_lower.ts), [check_declarations.ts](../src/core/check_declarations.ts), [world.ts](../src/core/validate/world.ts), [diagnostics.ts](../src/core/diagnostics.ts) |
-| Map and Set schema | The schema is `Schema.HashMap(key, value)` or `Schema.HashSet(element)`, at the sites where `Schema.Option` is used. The encoded side is a `HashMap` or a `HashSet` of encoded values, as the encoded side of `Schema.Option` is an `Option`. A JSON array does not decode into a `Map` or a `Set`: `decode` fails with `Expected HashMap` or `Expected HashSet`, and a host adapter must build the values. A conversion from entry arrays is out of scope. An inferred or checked entry reports the path of a bad entry, such as `["entries"][1][1]` for a `Map` value and `["values"][0]` for a `Set` element. An inferred input contract follows the `Option` cases | [types.ts](../src/core/emit/types.ts), [map_set_types_slow_test.ts](../tests/map_set_types_slow_test.ts) |
-| Map and Set equality | `HashMap` and `HashSet` use `Equal` and `Hash`. A record key matches another record with the same fields, so two keys built separately find one entry. `Hash.hash` caches the hash of each object, and `Equal.equals` caches the result of each outermost pair. The emitter does not freeze a record, so host code must not change an object after it is a key. `Equal` compares the key sets, so `{ a: 1 }` and `{ a: 1, b: undefined }` are not equal. Source construction and schema decoding both leave an absent optional field absent, so a decoded key and a source key with the same fields are equal and hash alike. The iteration order follows the hash structure, not the insertion order | [map_set_types_slow_test.ts](../tests/map_set_types_slow_test.ts) |
